60,3,1,talk,Minato,,A is too much work for everyone. B needs developers. C helps the clerks. D is too much for the staff.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,D is impossible because of the network coverage and visitor approval issues I found. B is out due to developer availability.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"A and C might have per-head licensing costs. B is a production unit, which sounds like a capital expense.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"A requires daily entry from everyone, which my research shows always fails. C is a narrow, specific tool.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,C solves the misrouted deliveries and the time lost to copying records. It is the most practical.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Midori, would C make the coordination group's life easier? Yes, it removes the need to hunt for addresses.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,C doesn't depend on customer plant networks. It's a safe bet technically.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"If C is a central repository, we can likely manage it as a fixed-fee project or within the software allowance.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"C is a standardization effort. While some failed, a searchable catalog is a narrow enough tool to succeed.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,It addresses the everyday losses I found. I strongly support C.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,I vote for C. It helps the people who are struggling with the workload.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. C is the only one that doesn't hit a technical wall. I vote C.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,It fits the budget constraints better than a new production studio. I vote C.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"It avoids the ""daily entry"" trap of A. I vote C.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,It fixes the floor's biggest headaches. I vote C.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
